# Going for Release

When the user says **Going for Release**, **Prep for release**, or a clear equivalent, run this ritual. Do **not** run it on ordinary commits or PRs.

## Versioning (hard rules — every prep)

These apply to **every** prep, including repeats on the same branch:

1. **Marketing version = branch semver.** Parse the leading `X.Y.Z` from the current branch name (`0.7.2-calendar-full-swipe` → `0.7.2`, `1.5.18-individualFixes` → `1.5.18`). Set Android `versionName` and iOS `MARKETING_VERSION` to that string. If the branch has no leading semver, ask once and stop.
2. **Always bump `versionCode`.** Increment Android `versionCode` and iOS `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` by **+1** from whatever is currently in the project — even when `versionName` is unchanged. Never rebuild/upload with the same `versionCode` as the previous prep. Play accepts any `versionName`; only `versionCode` must rise.

Do not skip the bump because “we already prepped this branch” or “only rebuilding the AAB.”

## Steps (fixed order — stop on failure)

| Step | Action | Stop if |
| ---- | ------ | ------- |
| 1 | Apply **Versioning** above (branch → `versionName` / `MARKETING_VERSION`; always `versionCode` / `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` +1). Prefer the project’s bump script when present (`npm run bump -- <X.Y.Z>` on Expenses — also writes `releases/vX.Y.Z.md`). Otherwise edit Android/iOS version fields directly and update store docs if the repo tracks them. | No semver and user did not supply one |
| 2 | Project CI / verify if defined (`npm run ci` on Expenses). Skip only when the repo has no equivalent. | Fails |
| 3 | Build signed release AAB with **host Gradle cache** (Expenses: `npm run release:aab`; Aura: `python3 run.py --aab` or `GRADLE_USER_HOME=$HOME/.gradle ./gradlew bundleRelease` after Fly-backed `build:mobile`). Use agent `required_permissions: ["all"]`. | Gradle/signing/verify error |
| 4 | **Release notes (when the repo has them):** confirm `releases/vX.Y.Z.md` exists; in the chat reply show both store paste blocks — **Android / Play Console** (`<en-US>…</en-US>`) and **iOS / App Store “What’s New”**. Do not paste the whole markdown file. On Aura (no `releases/` artifact yet), summarize user-facing changes in chat instead. | Expenses: missing `releases/vX.Y.Z.md` or empty store blocks |
| 5 | Before iOS ASC upload (Expenses): `npm run release:verify-ios-icon` (included in `npm run ci`) | Alpha channel on marketing icon |

## Release notes (Android + iOS)

When the project ships `releases/vX.Y.Z.md` (Expenses):

| Deliverable | Where |
| ----------- | ----- |
| Artifact | `releases/vX.Y.Z.md` (created by `npm run bump` via `scripts/release-notes.mjs`; see `releases/README.md`) |
| Shown in chat | Paste-ready **Play Console** block (Android) and **App Store What’s New** block (iOS) from that file |

If the artifact is missing after bump, run `npm run release:notes` and fix before finishing the ritual. Prefer user-facing bullets when editing notes; keep Play body ≤ 500 characters inside the language tags.

**Commit / push:** only when the user asks. If they do, run project CI first when defined. Include `releases/vX.Y.Z.md` in that commit when present.

## AD_ID gate (Expenses — required)

**Why:** Social Login / Play services merge ad permissions even though Expenses does not use ads.

**Source strip (keep):** `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` must still have `tools:node="remove"` on:

- `com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID`
- `android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_AD_ID`
- `android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_ATTRIBUTION`
- `android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_CUSTOM_AUDIENCE`
- `android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_TOPICS`

**After AAB build:** `npm run release:verify-ad-id` (or step 3 above) must pass — merged release manifest and AAB manifest contain **none** of those permissions.

- **Pass** → Play Data safety can stay **No advertising ID**.
- **Fail** → stop; fix strip lines or deps, rebuild.
- **Do not fail** solely because DEX still references `AdvertisingIdClient` (Social Login).

## Gradle execution policy (agent)

**Don’t AAB in the sandbox; do AAB with `all`.** That is the way around re-downloading Gradle every time.

- Run release AAB / `./gradlew` with **`required_permissions: ["all"]`** so `GRADLE_USER_HOME` (`~/.gradle`) persists.
- Prefer project wrappers (`android/gradlew`, or Aura `python3 run.py --aab` which forces `~/.gradle`).
- Always use the project `gradlew` (never bare `gradle` or re-init wrapper).
- **Do not** run `bundleRelease` in the default sandbox.

### Gradle download matrix

| What | Where | First run | Repeat (same Mac) | Agent sandbox | Agent `all` + `gradlew` |
| ---- | ----- | --------- | ----------------- | --------------- | ----------------------- |
| Wrapper (`gradle-*-all.zip`) | `~/.gradle/wrapper/dists/` | Once | Reused | Re-downloads each session | Reused |
| Maven / Google deps | `~/.gradle/caches/` | As needed | Mostly reused | Not persisted | Reused |
| Daemon JVM | Host background | Cold | Warm (`org.gradle.daemon=true`) | N/A | Warm after first build |
| Task outputs | `android/app/build/` + build cache | Full | Incremental | Thrown away | Persists |

**Symptom → cause:**

| You see | Likely cause |
| ------- | ------------ |
| “Downloading gradle-…-all.zip” every agent turn | Sandbox without `all`, or wrong `GRADLE_USER_HOME` |
| Slow, no wrapper download | Cold daemon, clean build, or dependency change |
| Android Studio fast, agent slow | Studio uses host cache; agent was sandboxed |

**Required:**

```sh
export GRADLE_USER_HOME="${GRADLE_USER_HOME:-$HOME/.gradle}"
cd android && ./gradlew bundleRelease
```

**Never:** bare `gradle`, re-init wrapper, or release builds in default sandbox.

**Sanity check:** `ls ~/.gradle/wrapper/dists/` shows the project’s wrapper dist after one successful build.

## iOS app icon gate (Expenses — required before ASC upload)

**Why:** App Store Connect rejects the 1024×1024 marketing icon if it has transparency or an alpha channel (error **90717**).

**Asset:** `ios/App/App/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/AppIcon-512@2x.png` must be **opaque RGB** (no alpha, no transparent pixels).

**Verify:** `npm run release:verify-ios-icon` (runs in `npm run ci`).

**Fix after updating icon art:** `npm run ios:flatten-icon` — composites onto plate color `#080814`, then re-verify.

**After icon fix:** Xcode **Product → Clean Build Folder**, re-**Archive**, upload (old archives still embed the bad icon).

## Out of scope (unless the user also asks)

Play Console upload, git tag, iOS archive/TestFlight, full ship-doc smoke.
